    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kenwood was platted outside Minneapolis in 1887, and a rail line ran along its west side near Cedar Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kenwoodmpls.org/neighborhood-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Advertised in the late 1880s as “high, sightly and attractive,” Kenwood was called the “choicest place for elegant residences.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kenwoodmpls.org/neighborhood-history",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake of the Isles was dredged in 1899 from a mosquito‑infested swamp, creating the islands and shoreline that now border Kenwood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kenwoodmpls.org/neighborhood-history",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kenwood’s historic mansions, built in early 20th‑century styles, are a hallmark of the neighborhood’s grand homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
